WEBVTT

00:02.160 --> 00:05.601
"It seems today that all you see

00:05.637 --> 00:09.041
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:09.125 --> 00:12.878
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.914 --> 00:14.964
"On which we used to rely?

00:15.714 --> 00:19.050
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:19.134 --> 00:24.139
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:24.264 --> 00:25.598
"Laugh and cry

00:25.723 --> 00:31.145
"He's a family guy

00:37.068 --> 00:41.154
Thanks for coming, Lois. Mark's wanted me
to see his one-man show for weeks.

00:41.238 --> 00:44.908
I think it's wonderful
you're supporting your old pal.

00:45.742 --> 00:47.911
Go long, Eddie. Go long.

00:47.947 --> 00:49.996
Further. Further!

00:50.121 --> 00:51.872
Ahhh...

00:51.997 --> 00:54.083
Life was crazy growing up in Brooklyn.

00:54.166 --> 00:58.045
We had some real characters in my
neighbourhood, like Frank the mailman.

00:58.128 --> 01:01.672
Hey, Mark.
The ants for your ant farm came today.

01:01.797 --> 01:03.967
And my friend Lonny - that knucklehead.

01:04.004 --> 01:06.471
Yo, Marky! Let's play some b-ball.

01:06.596 --> 01:10.014
B-ball. That's what we called it.

01:10.140 --> 01:12.725
And my grandma -
boy, was she somethin' else.

01:12.852 --> 01:18.146
Marky,
don't forget to take your cod-liver oil.

01:19.608 --> 01:23.902
What a piece of self-indulgent crap.
All the characters sounded the same.

01:23.985 --> 01:26.696
- Great show.
- You did me perfectly.

01:26.821 --> 01:28.990
Me too. You are so talented.

01:29.116 --> 01:32.869
That was awful. With practice
I could act circles around that guy.

01:32.952 --> 01:35.211
Oh, yeah? Well, put up or shut up.

01:35.247 --> 01:40.042
"This Thursday, auditions for
the Quahog School of Performing Arts. "

01:40.167 --> 01:42.961
- You should try out.
- That's not a bad idea, Lois.

01:43.087 --> 01:46.006
Ready for the best acting
you've seen all night?

01:46.089 --> 01:51.928
Mark! Wow, what a journey! Thank you.
Those three and a half hours just flew by.

01:54.138 --> 01:58.935
Hey, Santos, Pascoal. You've done such
good work today, I got a surprise for you.

01:59.018 --> 02:00.894
Doritos!

02:01.854 --> 02:03.188
Not now. Later.

02:14.242 --> 02:16.325
Help! Help!

02:16.450 --> 02:17.911
Oh, my God!

02:21.956 --> 02:26.333
Thank you. I was boogie-boarding
and I got sucked out by the riptide.

02:26.459 --> 02:30.088
- I thought I was a dead man.
- You gotta be starving. Eat these.

02:36.968 --> 02:39.596
My God! He was just floating
out there by himself?

02:39.679 --> 02:43.557
Yep. He was so grateful,
he invited us all over for dinner tonight.

02:43.643 --> 02:45.274
Good. I don't have to cook.

02:45.311 --> 02:48.772
Cook anyway and we'll throw it out.
I don't want you to get rusty.

02:49.064 --> 02:52.942
Peter, my audition's coming up.
Would you listen to my monologue?

02:53.026 --> 02:55.445
Sure, buddy. Let's hear it.

02:57.406 --> 03:01.576
- Julie, there's somethin' I gotta tell you...
- Ha! That's awesome. Go on.

03:01.701 --> 03:07.206
- Uh... tell you. I saw Dr Philips...
- Wow! Yes! Yes! I love it.

03:07.242 --> 03:10.923
...Dr Philips today.
I might not make it to Christmas.

03:10.959 --> 03:14.421
Oh, drop the bomb. There's not
a dry eye in the house. Keep goin'.

03:14.504 --> 03:17.340
No. I'm gonna stop.
Maybe we'll work on it later.

03:17.424 --> 03:21.385
Well, just so you know, it was good,
but I was also being generous.

03:24.096 --> 03:28.809
Well, you little jaybird! You wanna tell your
mommy and daddy the Griffins are here?

03:28.891 --> 03:31.186
Come on in.

03:31.311 --> 03:32.855
Welcome, Griffins.

03:32.891 --> 03:35.356
Oh... uh...

03:35.480 --> 03:39.028
- We must be early.
- Nonsense. You're right on time.

03:39.112 --> 03:42.990
Oh, my God! She's got hair growin'
out of her boobs and up to her head.

03:43.073 --> 03:45.491
You're, uh... You're completely...

03:45.576 --> 03:49.245
- Nude? Yes, we're nudists.
- Permission to freak out.

03:49.329 --> 03:52.665
- Peter, did you know this?
- I thought he lost his bathing suit.

03:52.790 --> 03:56.543
So you're the man who saved
my husband's life. Dottie Campbell.

03:56.626 --> 03:59.671
- What am I doing? Come here!
- Watch my hands, Lois.

03:59.754 --> 04:01.840
See where they are? No touchie.

04:01.965 --> 04:08.429
This is the back yard. That's premium
blue-tip Bermuda. Real hardy, but soft.

04:08.513 --> 04:11.013
- Good Lord.
- Don't look directly into it, Lois.

04:11.139 --> 04:14.351
The hot dogs and burgers are ready.
Can I get you a beer, Peter?

04:14.476 --> 04:17.394
- What do you got?
- I've got Busch.

04:17.478 --> 04:18.730
Oh, and Busch Light.

04:18.855 --> 04:21.650
Sounds like Jeff's home.

04:21.775 --> 04:24.904
- Hey, sport! How'd you do?
- I got first place, Dad.

04:24.986 --> 04:29.573
Way to go, champ. Jeff plays
varsity tennis for Saint Genevieve High.

04:29.698 --> 04:32.618
- Cool.
- Is this the biggest thing you've ever seen?

04:32.701 --> 04:36.580
Don't get too cocky. I had a big one
like that when I was your age.

04:36.663 --> 04:40.542
You were a show-off yourself, Dave.
You brought it out on our first date.

04:40.624 --> 04:43.044
Lois, I'm scared. Oh, I'll get that.

04:43.127 --> 04:44.170
Hey!

04:44.297 --> 04:47.297
Oh, God! Oh, Dave, sorry! Oh, God!

04:49.091 --> 04:52.428
- Boobies!
- That's enough. I'm glad to be out of there.

04:52.511 --> 04:55.347
What those people are doing
just ain't natural.

04:55.431 --> 04:57.517
- Boobies!
- Did you hear me, young man?

04:57.641 --> 05:00.644
- What was the big deal? They were nice.
- Boobies!

05:00.681 --> 05:02.520
- Peter.
- Do it.

05:04.940 --> 05:09.193
- Did you have fun at the circus today, Chris?
- Elephants are bigger in person.

05:15.032 --> 05:18.577
- Break a leg up there, Brian.
- You seem awfully enthusiastic.

05:18.702 --> 05:23.164
At first I wanted you to fail. But then
I realised you'd be out five days a week,

05:23.289 --> 05:26.291
which means I'd be free to throw
some of my sexy parties.

05:37.553 --> 05:39.972
- Brian Griffin.
- Good luck, Brian.

05:40.056 --> 05:44.768
Hi. I'm Brian Griffin, and this is
from John Waltz's Leaving Wichita.

05:47.063 --> 05:50.190
Julie, there's somethin' I gotta tell you.

05:50.273 --> 05:54.360
I saw Dr Philips today.
I might not make it to Christmas.

05:54.443 --> 05:56.946
- Thank you. Next.
- Next?

05:57.071 --> 05:59.365
Hold on, Brian. Stay up there.

05:59.783 --> 06:03.744
See here! Brian Griffin is a brilliant actor
with talent and passion.

06:03.827 --> 06:06.539
But you alleged experts
obviously didn't notice.

06:06.664 --> 06:10.625
Well, I did notice.
I saw a man bare his soul up here.

06:10.708 --> 06:13.628
His pain ran through my heart
like an errant locomotive.

06:13.753 --> 06:16.672
But it was wasted. Wasted on all of you!

06:18.340 --> 06:21.760
Well, it looks like we have to
reconsider. Brian, we want you...

06:21.796 --> 06:23.762
- Yes!
... off the stage.

06:23.845 --> 06:27.931
But your young friend would be perfect
for our rising-star programme.

06:28.016 --> 06:31.352
Splendid! This calls for a sexy party.

06:39.694 --> 06:42.530
OK, funcakes, let's do a scene.

06:42.613 --> 06:46.908
Stewie, how about you and, let's see...
one of our veterans... Olivia.

06:46.992 --> 06:49.911
I'm not doing a scene with him.
He's inexperienced.

06:50.036 --> 06:52.123
He'll drag my whole performance down.

06:52.206 --> 06:54.498
Are you serious? Is she serious?

06:54.623 --> 06:57.625
OK, Stewie, I'll give you a solo exercise.

06:58.044 --> 07:02.006
You're gonna do an exercise we call
"The Life Cycle". Without using words,

07:02.131 --> 07:06.176
you're gonna act out your entire life
from birth to death as I describe it.

07:06.213 --> 07:08.642
Ready? Lie down.

07:08.679 --> 07:13.683
Now you're being born. Ready?
And burst through the placenta!

07:13.808 --> 07:18.189
Now fast-forward. It's your first day of school.
You're alone and scared.

07:18.272 --> 07:21.732
But it's all right. It's Sloppy Joe day.

07:21.816 --> 07:25.569
Pull it back. The lady touched the bun
and she's not wearing gloves.

07:25.694 --> 07:29.239
Fast-forward. You're a businessman,
you manage a lot of people.

07:29.322 --> 07:33.493
Here comes Henderson.
He lost the big account. You're mad.

07:33.618 --> 07:35.912
Madder. Madder!

07:35.995 --> 07:38.206
Come on. Hot, hot.
There it is. You got it.

07:38.289 --> 07:41.897
And fast-forward. You're an old man now.
You're on your deathbed.

07:41.933 --> 07:45.504
Your son is holding your hand.
You tell him you accept his lifestyle

07:45.588 --> 07:50.301
and regret humiliating him at his sister's
wedding by calling him your other daughter.

07:50.384 --> 07:53.513
And... scene. OK, any comments?

07:55.388 --> 07:58.308
You are the weakest link. Goodbye.

07:59.558 --> 08:03.939
Ha, ha, ha! Oh, gosh, that's funny.
That's really funny.

08:03.976 --> 08:06.023
Do you write your own material?

08:06.148 --> 08:09.483
That is so fresh.
"You are the weakest link. Goodbye. "

08:09.567 --> 08:13.530
I've never heard anyone make
that joke before. You're the first.

08:13.655 --> 08:17.617
I've never heard anyone reference that
outside the programme before.

08:17.701 --> 08:22.043
That's what she says on the show, right?
"You are the weakest link. Goodbye. "

08:22.079 --> 08:29.085
You've taken that and used it out of context
to insult me in this everyday situation.

08:29.168 --> 08:32.679
What a clever, smart girl you must be

08:32.716 --> 08:35.632
to come up with a joke like that
all by yourself.

08:35.759 --> 08:37.844
Mm. That's so fresh, too.

08:37.927 --> 08:40.430
Any Titanic jokes you want to throw at me

08:40.555 --> 08:44.808
while we're hitting these phenomena
at the height of their popularity?

08:44.933 --> 08:46.811
Cos I'm here.

08:46.894 --> 08:48.980
God, you're so funny!

08:52.234 --> 08:55.150
- Meg?
- Jeff! Wow, hey!

08:55.234 --> 08:58.782
- What are you doing here?
- They had a sale on Super Soakers.

09:00.865 --> 09:02.117
Agh! What the heck...?

09:02.242 --> 09:05.578
- Nudist!
- My dad's a tailor, you jerk!

09:06.079 --> 09:10.041
- Gosh, that's awful.
- That's all right. I'm used to it.

09:10.166 --> 09:14.419
I'd better go. So, um... would you
wanna do something sometime?

09:14.543 --> 09:19.007
- Sure. That'd be great.
- Cool. I'll call you later.

09:27.680 --> 09:31.312
Holy moly! It must be my birthday.

09:43.738 --> 09:46.949
Thank you. Thank you. That was, um...

09:47.074 --> 09:51.037
"Me Farting" by Chopin.

09:52.163 --> 09:55.708
Thank you. Thank you very...

10:00.210 --> 10:04.383
- So, Olivia. Beautiful day.
- You're not gonna fart again, are you?

10:05.925 --> 10:10.096
Well, I'd love to stay and chat,
but you're a total bitch.

10:16.476 --> 10:19.688
The quarterly review's tomorrow.
Think your kids will pass?

10:19.812 --> 10:23.651
I'll tell you who won't.
It starts with an O and rhymes with Bolivia.

10:23.687 --> 10:26.152
- Give up? Olivia.
- Really?

10:26.276 --> 10:29.196
She's such a frosty box.
She won't work with anybody.

10:29.279 --> 10:33.661
Stewie Griffin is also on the fence.
If he and Olivia don't deliver at their reviews,

10:33.786 --> 10:36.996
I'll have to kick their
cute little bottoms out of here.

10:41.375 --> 10:44.419
This table is reserved for people with talent.

10:44.503 --> 10:48.381
Stow the 'tude, queenie.
You and I have a problem. Read it and weep.

10:48.464 --> 10:51.926
- "Doesn't work well with others"?
- Mine's no better.

10:52.009 --> 10:56.931
I'll spare you the details, but the phrase
"garden variety" appears a number of times.

10:57.014 --> 10:59.935
- What am I going to do?
- What are we going to do?

11:00.060 --> 11:03.479
Our evaluation's tomorrow.
You need someone to work with,

11:03.515 --> 11:05.898
and I need someone to make me look good.

11:05.981 --> 11:08.190
- I don't know.
- Fine. Refuse my offer.

11:08.273 --> 11:11.110
Get booted out
and wind up like Linda Evans.

11:11.194 --> 11:15.907
Linda Evans, we have a spill in aisle 9.
Linda Evans, a spill in aisle 9.

11:17.992 --> 11:21.537
- Do you like yours with crust or without?
- How do you like yours?

11:21.620 --> 11:25.499
Let's both answer at the same time.
One, two, three.

11:25.583 --> 11:26.625
- Without.
- Without.

11:26.750 --> 11:29.711
Holy moly! That's eight things
we have in common.

11:29.748 --> 11:32.637
- Kids, we're home.
- Hello, Mr and Mrs Griffin.

11:32.673 --> 11:36.134
- You remember Jeff?
- Sure. Lois, I'm gonna borrow your mace.

11:36.217 --> 11:37.802
Agh! That's better.

11:37.885 --> 11:41.221
Meg, did any of the neighbours
see Jeff come over?

11:41.346 --> 11:43.849
Mom! Come on, Jeff.
Let's go in the other room.

11:43.932 --> 11:46.643
Now, Meg, no need to get so testes... testy.

11:46.768 --> 11:48.854
Oh, nuts... I mean crap!

11:48.937 --> 11:52.691
- You wanna sit down?
- Wait a second. Don't sit down yet.

11:52.816 --> 11:56.778
- Dad, what are you doing?
- I'm, uh... keepin' the couch fresh.

11:56.861 --> 11:58.285
- Dad!
- It's OK, Meg.

11:58.321 --> 12:00.948
I understand what's goin' on. I'm gonna go.

12:01.031 --> 12:04.075
Oh! Just step on these coasters
on your way out.

12:04.158 --> 12:08.330
Don't step on the hot lava.
The carpet is hot lava.

12:09.581 --> 12:11.213
I can't believe you guys!

12:11.250 --> 12:13.960
How could you bring
that naked kid to our house?

12:13.996 --> 12:16.796
Because I like him. He remembers my name.

12:16.879 --> 12:20.968
I'm sorry, honey, but we don't think
you should see him any more.

12:22.301 --> 12:24.513
I hate the sound of her cryin'.

12:24.596 --> 12:27.307
You know what sounds even worse?

12:27.344 --> 12:29.599
Ahh! Listen to that.

12:30.851 --> 12:33.143
Don't you hate that?

12:33.269 --> 12:35.647
That is awful.

12:35.772 --> 12:40.234
I think it's easier on me
cos I'm the one makin' the sound.

12:43.361 --> 12:47.116
Nice effort, Brad. But let's remember
our performance hierarchy:

12:47.241 --> 12:51.203
Legitimate theatre, musical,
stand-up, ventriloquism, magic, mime.

12:51.287 --> 12:55.165
Next up is Olivia. Liv, what monologue
are you doing for us this time?

12:55.248 --> 12:58.168
I'm not doing a monologue.
I'm doing a piece with Stewie.

12:58.204 --> 13:00.670
A duet? Really? Let's see it.

13:01.629 --> 13:03.799
Five, six, seven, eight.

13:06.300 --> 13:09.846
- " Who's got the greatest gal around?
- " You do

13:09.971 --> 13:13.390
- " Who's got the sweetest man in town?
- " You do

13:13.516 --> 13:17.769
"Who's got a guy
who makes her smile all day?

13:17.894 --> 13:20.480
By the way, I'm not so bad to look at either.

13:20.605 --> 13:24.025
- " Who's got a guy with lots of brains?
- " You do

13:24.150 --> 13:27.570
- " Who's got a girl who loves chow mein?
- " You do

13:27.695 --> 13:30.406
"Who's got the greatest love in the world?

13:30.489 --> 13:32.366
- " You do
- " And you do

13:32.493 --> 13:34.034
"Thank goodness I've got you

13:34.159 --> 13:37.642
- " Who's got a guy to tell her jokes?
- " You do

13:37.678 --> 13:41.124
- " Who's got a girl to show the folks?
- " You do

13:41.249 --> 13:44.876
"Who's got a girl
he'd like to one day undress?

13:45.002 --> 13:48.965
"Give it a rest -
I told you not until we're married

13:49.048 --> 13:52.510
- " Who's got the gal with all the snazz?
- " You do

13:52.593 --> 13:56.139
- " Who's got the fella with pizzazz?
- " You do

13:56.263 --> 14:00.517
"Who's got the greatest love in the world?

14:00.642 --> 14:05.231
- " You do
- " And you do

14:05.268 --> 14:09.817
"Thank goodness I've got you

14:12.612 --> 14:14.822
Watch this. Are you watching?

14:15.657 --> 14:18.368
That's for me ever having
doubted you. A-plus!

14:19.076 --> 14:23.371
That's for you wearing purple pants
with blue socks. Eww!

14:23.455 --> 14:25.248
I totally called him on it.

14:29.294 --> 14:33.047
No secrets. I wanna share
Stewie and Olivia with the world.

14:33.083 --> 14:36.175
They're awfully young.
Is this really a good idea?

14:36.300 --> 14:39.845
It's a great idea. I've always
dreamed of becoming an actress.

14:39.928 --> 14:43.597
That's not why I'm pushing Olivia.
Is it suspicious that I said that?

14:43.681 --> 14:45.731
Well, I guess it might be OK.

14:45.767 --> 14:49.853
Sure, Lois. Look at Elroy Jetson. He was
a child actor and he turned out fine.

14:50.982 --> 14:54.234
Do you know who I am? I'm Elroy Jetson.

14:54.317 --> 14:56.735
Yeah, yeah. Come back
when you have some money.

14:56.819 --> 14:59.238
- Take him home, Bamm-Bamm.
- Bamm-Bamm, bam!

14:59.321 --> 15:02.657
I don't wanna go home.
Take me to Astro's grave.

15:04.535 --> 15:06.743
- " You do
- " And you do

15:06.827 --> 15:13.835
"Thank goodness I've got you

15:20.299 --> 15:22.383
Do you hear that? They love us!

15:22.466 --> 15:25.512
- Yes, we're a hit. You were amazing.
- So were you.

15:25.595 --> 15:28.894
It was a good crowd. They didn't
notice you missed that F sharp.

15:28.931 --> 15:33.436
- Yes, well... Beg pardon?
- The F sharp, darling. You were slightly off.

15:33.520 --> 15:36.126
- I'm sure I wasn't.
- Well, maybe it was me.

15:36.162 --> 15:38.732
- Must've been you.
- I was being sarcastic.

15:38.857 --> 15:41.443
- Well, it wasn't me.
- Well, it wasn't me.

15:48.116 --> 15:49.785
Like this. Listen to me.

15:52.286 --> 15:54.497
Hi, Meg.

15:55.831 --> 15:59.549
Peter, was it unfair of us to tell Meg
she couldn't see that boy?

15:59.586 --> 16:05.341
Completely. We totally reamed her. Did you
see that look in her eyes? She hates you.

16:11.387 --> 16:15.433
There it is, kids. Your first marquee.
Meet you inside.

16:17.935 --> 16:20.229
- Exciting.
- The marquee or the other thing?

16:20.354 --> 16:23.566
- What other thing?
- The sex... with Simon.

16:23.691 --> 16:26.694
- Why else would your name be first?
- It's obvious.

16:26.819 --> 16:30.655
Lead with strength, put your best foot
forward, et cetera, et cetera.

16:30.780 --> 16:32.241
So the sex was good?

16:32.325 --> 16:36.286
- Shut up, you egotistical jerk.
- You shut up, you sack-bellied strumpet!

16:36.411 --> 16:38.998
- Blimp-headed jackass!
- Mealy-mouthed crotch pheasant!

16:39.123 --> 16:46.212
"Thank goodness I've got you

16:49.423 --> 16:52.676
Jeff! What are you doing here?
I'm not supposed to see you.

16:52.759 --> 16:55.387
- Your parents invited me.
- But they wouldn't...

16:55.470 --> 16:58.181
- Yes, we would.
- Oh, my God! What are you doing?!

16:58.306 --> 17:01.643
We were wrong, Meg. If you like Jeff,
we should give him a chance.

17:01.726 --> 17:04.019
We wanted him to feel welcome in our home.

17:04.143 --> 17:06.938
Mom, I need new batteries for my Walkman.

17:07.063 --> 17:09.983
Hey! Why is everybody else naked?

17:11.318 --> 17:13.366
Yahtzee! I win!

17:13.402 --> 17:16.656
Yeah! In your face! In your face! In your face!

17:17.908 --> 17:21.036
- I gotta go. Thanks, Mr and Mrs Griffin.
- Our pleasure.

17:21.119 --> 17:22.495
Nice hanging with you.

17:22.578 --> 17:27.501
- I hope my parents didn't embarrass you.
- Are you kidding? I think they're great.

17:27.583 --> 17:31.462
It took a lot of guts for them to do that.
I'll see you later.

17:33.003 --> 17:35.090
Thanks, you guys. That was really cool.

17:35.215 --> 17:39.052
Peter, can I borrow your lawn mower?
Agh... You got a towel?

17:39.177 --> 17:43.014
Simon, would you be a dear and ask Stewie
to dance on his own feet tonight?

17:43.139 --> 17:46.769
Could you provide Olivia with a bucket
so she can carry a tune?

17:46.805 --> 17:48.853
People, stop this craziness!

17:48.978 --> 17:53.649
The Providence Journal's critic is here.
If we get a good review, the doors'll fly open.

17:53.686 --> 17:55.734
Go get 'em, my little silly-billies.

17:55.859 --> 17:58.236
- Let's just get through this.
- Fine with me.

17:58.361 --> 18:03.575
Wait a minute. You're wearing ruby lipstick.
You're painted up like some jezebel.

18:03.659 --> 18:07.120
You're one to talk. You've been
stuffing your diaper since day one.

18:07.203 --> 18:09.287
It's where I keep my peppermint Mentos.

18:09.412 --> 18:14.084
Just because your breath reeks of rotten
Lunchables doesn't mean mine has to.

18:29.013 --> 18:31.147
Break it up! Break it up!

18:31.183 --> 18:36.606
I don't need this act and I don't need you.
You've done nothing but hold me back. I quit!

18:36.730 --> 18:39.109
All I've held you back from is failure.

18:39.234 --> 18:41.942
Come on, Simon.
We don't need that Bebe No-worth.

18:42.025 --> 18:46.948
I don't know, Stewie. Without Olivia, this act
is like Fire Island after Labor Day: Over.

18:47.031 --> 18:49.867
Fine. I don't need you.
I can manage my own career.

18:49.951 --> 18:53.079
Yes. Yes, I'm quite capable of that.

18:58.710 --> 19:01.754
"I've got my top hat and cane

19:01.837 --> 19:07.050
"And a pocketful of miracles,
pocketful of miracles

19:09.053 --> 19:12.055
- Somebody get a hook!
- This is worse than Seussical!

19:12.091 --> 19:14.764
No, wait. I was about to do this thing.

19:22.606 --> 19:24.693
Oh, hello. Didn't notice you there.

19:24.776 --> 19:28.862
It's not easy living with my family.
Bunch of characters, they are.

19:28.945 --> 19:34.157
Like my father. "Holy crap, Lois.
Check out the freakin' log in the toilet. "

19:34.193 --> 19:36.368
Get off the stage!

19:38.954 --> 19:41.874
What do you say, Bernie?
Two nights at the old rate?

19:41.999 --> 19:45.210
I told you before, kid,
I can't book you without Olivia.

19:45.335 --> 19:48.719
But that's the good news.
We're back together. She's here.

19:48.755 --> 19:54.094
Hi, Bernie. Glad to be back.
Ask Stewie about his sexy parties.

19:55.011 --> 19:58.347
"Ask Stewie about his sexy parties. "
What were you thinking?

19:58.472 --> 20:00.139
- I was...
- I'm not speaking to you.

20:00.222 --> 20:01.268
- But...
- Shut up!

20:03.560 --> 20:07.857
I guess the best advice I got
was from Marty Scorsese.

20:07.940 --> 20:11.609
I was having a problem understanding
why I'd been taking abuse

20:11.693 --> 20:15.029
from this lower-ranking officer
played by Chris O'Donnell.

20:15.154 --> 20:20.034
And... he told me "You don't have to
understand it. Your character does. "

20:20.159 --> 20:21.910
That always stuck with me.

20:22.036 --> 20:24.585
- Stewie?
- Olivia! What are you doing here?

20:24.621 --> 20:28.375
I must be an absolute mess.
The studio made me fire my make-up girl.

20:28.500 --> 20:34.422
I just wanted to stop by and see how
you were doing. I heard some things...

20:34.547 --> 20:36.925
That it's going great for me? You heard right.

20:37.050 --> 20:40.053
- Glad to hear that.
- But, hey... um...

20:40.179 --> 20:44.556
If you're not busy... what say
you and I get the old team back together?

20:44.640 --> 20:48.101
Well, actually, I can't.
I'm on my way to Hollywood.

20:48.185 --> 20:52.272
- I got this part in a movie and...
- Oh, oh, oh, oh... What am I thinking?

20:52.354 --> 20:55.902
I'd love to, but I just... I'm booked solid.

20:56.027 --> 20:59.237
I'm doing a three-episode guest shot
on The Gilmore Girls.

20:59.362 --> 21:02.782
I play Rory's motorcycle-driving boyfriend.

21:02.907 --> 21:06.744
He's a bad boy at heart,
but there's some good in there, Olivia.

21:06.869 --> 21:08.955
And it comes through absolutely.

21:09.039 --> 21:13.417
That's really good to hear, Stewie.
Please, take care of yourself.

21:16.128 --> 21:18.004
See you on the coast.

21:19.382 --> 21:23.759
- So, did you let him have it?
- No. He let himself have it.

21:26.345 --> 21:28.430
This is it.

21:30.849 --> 21:32.810
Hey. How ya doin', kid?

21:32.935 --> 21:37.105
- Are you from Wardrobe?
- No, it's Brian. I brought what you wanted.

21:37.188 --> 21:41.777
- But they won't let me leave it so...
- Hit it once. Please, just once.

21:44.485 --> 21:46.364
Oh, my God. I was flat.

21:46.400 --> 21:48.242
Help me up. Let's go home.

21:48.243 --> 22:49.243
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru